    setup: {
      players: 'Three players. A standard 52-card pack without jokers is used. Cards in each suit rank from high to low A, K, Q, J, 10, 9, 8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2. Clubs are always trumps; hearts, diamonds and spades are plain suits. Deal and play are clockwise; the turn to deal passes to the left after each hand.',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card pack without jokers.',
      equipment: 'Cards only.',
      dealing: 'Dealer deals all 52 cards one at a time into four hands of 13: one for each player and one spare bid hand face down in the center. Each player may in turn (left of dealer to dealer) exchange their hand for the bid hand; last exchanger leads to the first trick, otherwise left of dealer leads.',
    },
    turnFlow: 'Clubs are always trumps. Follow suit if possible; if possible you must play a card that beats the highest card so far in the trick. You may not lead a club until clubs are broken or you have only clubs. Trick won by highest club in it, or if no club by highest card of the suit led. Winner of each trick leads to the next.',
